  "scope_finding": "Current orders/trades specs identify authenticated-user scope but do not define cross-credential lifecycle coverage for revoked/deleted owner credentials. SDKs implement authenticated GET filters and pagination; this does not establish backend authorization semantics. Documented Session Key restrictions remain distinct from already closed historical gaps.",
  "watermark_finding": "Official Python and TypeScript settlement helpers poll known AcceptedOrder trade IDs until CONFIRMED/FAILED. Timeout is a client timeout, not a server queue-drain guarantee. Data v2 status reports chain ingestion and serving projections, not a CLOB pending cancellation/match/retry/fee/settlement barrier. Accounting snapshot specification lists positions.csv/equity.csv without a complete pending-liability guarantee. Exchange code settles supplied signed orders and exposes status by hash, not an enumerable offchain queue.",
  "interface_limitations": [
    "Data API /v2/status, /v2/openapi.json and /v1/accounting/snapshot returned HTTP 403 from this environment; their documented semantics were reviewed, no access restriction bypass attempted.",
    "No universal impossibility claim: conclusion applies to documented public contracts and interfaces actually accessible in this audit.",
    "Public repository inventory reviewed (103 repositories); relevant official Python/TypeScript SDKs and CTF Exchange V2 source pinned by Git SHA. No public backend coverage/queue-drain guarantee established."
  ],
  "fresh_account_artifact": "analysis/legacy_settlement_observation_1791125668713.json",
  "fresh_account_summary": {
    "cash_raw": "109160000",
    "visible_orders": 0,
    "visible_trades": 0,
    "visible_positions": 0,
    "accessible_pagination_exhausted": true,
